.\" -*- coding: UTF-8 -*-
.TH SWPASSKEYD 1 "2026-11-04" "swpasskey 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
swpasskeyd \- TPM-backed virtual FIDO2 authenticator with desktop confirmation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swpasskeyd
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B swpasskeyd
creates a virtual FIDO HID device through Linux UHID. Browsers can use it as a
security key for WebAuthn registration and authentication. The Debian user
service uses TPM-backed signing keys and desktop notifications with Allow and
Deny buttons. The browser handles the CTAP PIN prompt; the notification confirms
user presence. A browser may cache a PIN verification token for a limited time.
.PP
This is a software authenticator. PIN verification and presence confirmation
are not enforced by TPM hardware. Same-user malware may use TPM keys even
though it cannot directly extract the private keys. Keep an independent account
recovery method.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-help
Show command help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Print the upstream program version and exit. Use dpkg-query to see the Debian
package revision.
.TP
.BI \-\-key-backend= backend
Select auto, se, tpm, or software. On Linux, auto may fall back to software.
The Debian service explicitly selects tpm and fails if TPM is unavailable.
The se backend is for macOS.
.TP
.BI \-\-store " path"
Use a different credential store.
.TP
.BI \-\-ctl-socket " path"
Use a different Unix control socket. Overrides SWPASSKEY_CTL_SOCKET.
.TP
.B \-\-dek-file
Keep the store encryption key in a mode-0600 sidecar file instead of the desktop
keyring. This is not additional PIN protection.
.TP
.B \-\-testing
Request automatic presence approval for development. Refused by this Debian
release build. Never use automatic approval for real credentials.
.SH DEBIAN SERVICE
The service runs as the logged-in user, not root. XDG autostart starts it at
graphical login. Avoid running another daemon against the same store.
.PP
.nf
systemctl --user status swpasskeyd.service
systemctl --user restart swpasskeyd.service
journalctl --user -u swpasskeyd.service -b
swpasskeyctl stats
.fi
.PP
After first installation, reboot to load UHID and apply active-seat device
permissions. Check that stats reports the TPM backend and the journal contains
presence_notify_ready. Notifications must support actions. Do Not Disturb may
hide them. If no notification backend is available, the daemon falls back to
stdin; the service has no interactive stdin, so requests time out without approval.
.PP
Disable the swpasskey entry in desktop autostart settings to disable login
startup. systemctl --user disable alone does not disable the XDG entry.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SWPASSKEY_LOG
error, warn, info, or debug.
.TP
.B SWPASSKEY_PRESENCE
Use auto, stdin, or notify on Linux. The Debian service sets notify.
.TP
.B SWPASSKEY_TPM_TCTI
TPM transport, normally device:/dev/tpmrm0; fixed by the Debian service.
.TP
.B SWPASSKEY_CTL_SOCKET
Override the control socket unless --ctl-socket is supplied.
.TP
.BR XDG_DATA_HOME ", " XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Select data and runtime directory bases.
.TP
.BR SWPASSKEY_TESTING ", " SWPASSKEY_HID_SOCKET ", " SWPASSKEY_TPM_UNSAFE_NOTPMRM
Development controls for automatic approval, socket transport instead of UHID,
and unsafe TPM transport respectively. Do not use for normal operation. The
Debian service disables or removes these overrides.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/swpasskey/credentials.bin
Credential store. Without XDG_DATA_HOME, uses ~/.local/share/swpasskey/credentials.bin.
The desktop keyring normally holds the store encryption key; upstream can fall
back to a mode-0600 sidecar file if the keyring is unavailable.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/swpasskey/ctl.sock
Default control socket. Without XDG_RUNTIME_DIR, uses the data directory.
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/autostart/swpasskey.desktop
Graphical login startup entry.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/swpasskeyd.service
Packaged user service. Use systemctl --user edit for local overrides.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/70-swpasskey.rules
Access rules for the active local user. UHID access permits virtual HID creation.
.SH NOTES
Removing the package does not remove user credentials or revoke website passkeys.
Do not clear the TPM or delete the store as a troubleshooting step: credentials
may become unusable. Stop the service before removing the package.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR swpasskeyctl (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
.PP
https://github.com/madeye/swpasskey
